        "original_id": "e676efd5-354c-5f2f-bc2c-c07431744752",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Maria Callas, Vincenzo Bellini, John Ardoin\n- Roles: opera soprano, opera composer, music critic\n- Topics: opera repertoire, bel canto, opera seria\n\nFacts:\n- Vincenzo Bellini was an Italian opera composer born on 3 November 1801 and died on 23 September 1835.\n- Vincenzo Bellini was known for long-flowing melodic lines and was called \"the Swan of Catania.\"\n- Maria Callas's early career repertoire included Wagner's music dramas.\n- Maria Callas's repertoire ranged from classical opera seria to bel canto operas by Donizetti, Bellini, and Rossini, and also included works by Verdi and Puccini.\n- John Ardoin was born on January 8, 1935, in Alexandria, Louisiana, and died on March 18, 2001, in San José, Costa Rica.\n- John Ardoin was the music critic of The Dallas Morning News for thirty-two years.\n- John Ardoin was known for his friendship with Maria Callas, his encyclopedic knowledge of her work, and for writing four books about her.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
